{
 "translation": "It is not known whether this matter was right or wrong, but according to the decision of scholars, conferences were held at a high level here and there, and finally, one day, it was decided for the exchange of lunatics. After a thorough investigation, those Muslim lunatics whose relatives were still in India were allowed to stay there. The remaining ones were sent to the border. Here in Pakistan, since almost all Hindus and Sikhs had already left, the question of keeping anyone did not even arise. All the Hindu-Sikh lunatics were sent to the border under police protection.",
